1. `data_source_json` seed shape is not canonical serde for `DataSource::WorkspaceFile`. Packet seeds `{"kind":"workspace_file","name":{"kind":"inbox"}}` etc. [L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md:80), [L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md:88). Actual `DataSource` is externally tagged with only `rename_all`, and `WorkspaceFile { kind }` is the variant. [source.rs](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/src-tauri/abilities-runtime/src/abilities/provenance/source.rs:71), [source.rs](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/src-tauri/abilities-runtime/src/abilities/provenance/source.rs:81). Use serde-produced JSON, e.g. `{"workspace_file":{"kind":"inbox"}}`.

2. Category seed count conflicts with locked contract. Wave plan says defaults are all six categories for the per-entity registry. [v1.4.5-waves.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:534). Packet seeds person with only four, omitting `presentations` and `contracts`. [L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md:104). This makes done-when “all default pairs” ambiguous/incomplete. [L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md:185).

3. Trait/import compileability is underspecified: packet signature references bare `EntityType` and `CategoryNotAllowed`. [L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md:34). Existing canonical `EntityType` is `crate::entity::EntityType`. [entity.rs](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/src-tauri/src/entity.rs:13). `CategoryNotAllowed` only appears as a future `PlacementError` variant, not a registry error type. [v1.4.5-waves.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:937).

4. Security negative fixtures miss the packet’s own strict-child root-equality case. Contract says canonical path must be a strict child, no equality with root. [L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md:128). Fixture list has traversal, absolute path, symlink, race, but no workspace-root path/directory rejection. [L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md:142).

5. Stale lint marker: packet tells allowlist exceptions to use `dos-146-allowed`, not DOS-464 or a neutral marker. [L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W1-B-DOS-464.md:151). This is inherited from wave text. [v1.4.5-waves.md](/private/tmp/dailyos-v145-w1a/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:542).

